Hi<%= " #{@user.name.split.first}" if @user.name.present? %>,

You signed up for Pairin a while ago, and I'd guess it didn't do much for you. That's on me: it asked you to book a call with a stranger before you'd exchanged a word.

So I've changed it. You post what you want to learn, someone applies, and you talk in the app first. If it's a good fit, you both say yes and get a shared Workspace to keep going in. If it isn't, nobody's the worse for it. No time slots, no intro calls.

<% if @paused_searches.size == 1 -%>
I've switched off your old search, "<%= @paused_searches.first.subject %>", so nobody applies to something you've forgotten about. If you're still looking, it takes one click to switch it back on:
<% elsif @paused_searches.size > 1 -%>
I've switched off your old searches, so nobody applies to something you've forgotten about. If you're still looking, it takes one click to switch one back on:
<% elsif @has_on_search -%>
Your search is still on, so there's nothing you need to do. You can see it here:
<% else -%>
If you still want someone to learn with, posting a search takes about a minute:
<% end -%>
<%= @action_url %>

<% if @user.date_of_birth.blank? -%>
The first time you sign in, we'll ask for your date of birth. It's a one-time step.

<% end -%>
If it's not for you, that's fine too. And if you try it and something's off, reply to this email. I read them.

Jovica

